<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef unevenly steady on mostly moderate demand and offerings.  Select and Choice rib and loin cuts weak, while round and chuck cuts steady to firm. Beef trimmings generally steady on mostly moderate demand and light to moderate offerings. - USDA</p>
<p>-----</p>
<p>269 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p> 47 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>43 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =	99.26	 99.04	 92.76	 92.51</p>
<p>Changes	  -0.22	 -0.30	 -0.28	 -0.15</p>
<p>Rib	  155.82	153.94	147.56	147.74</p>
<p>Chuck	 66.91	 65.90	 66.81	 65.46</p>
<p>Round	 83.54	 83.54	 81.98	 81.98</p>
<p>Loin	 160.80	162.12	136.37	137.01</p>
<p>Brisket     56.83	 56.83	 56.17	 56.17</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  63.74	 63.66	 63.96	 63.80</p>
<p>Flank	 58.52	 58.52	 57.59	 57.59</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
